Project-CarpeDiem
=================

CarpeDiem is a clean and stable Android experience, built for everyday use.
Simple, fast, and respectful of your device. Version 1.0, codename Initium,
based on LineageOS `lineage-24.0` (Android 17).

Highlights
----------
* CarpeDiem versioning (`1.0 - Initium`), maintainer and package-type display
* Rising-style blurred bottom search bar, time-based greetings, wallpaper device card
* Ornatus customizations hub, QuickSwitch multi-launcher support
* Pixel apps and launcher on GMS builds, vanilla by default
* Dual shade preference, background blur, advanced restart by default

Getting started
---------------

To get started with CarpeDiem, you'll need to get familiar with [Source Control Tools](https://source.android.com/setup/develop).

To initialize your local repository using the CarpeDiem trees, use a command like this:
```
repo init -u https://github.com/Project-CarpeDiem/android.git -b seventeen --git-lfs
```
Then to sync up:
```
repo sync
```
CarpeDiem is based on LineageOS `lineage-24.0` (tracked on branch `seventeen`). See `snippets/carpediem.xml`
for the repositories CarpeDiem forks; everything else tracks upstream.

Build Flags
-----------
```
# Maintainer Name
CARPEDIEM_MAINTAINER := "YourInput" (Default: Unknown)

# Chipset Marketing Name For About Specs
CARPEDIEM_CHIPSET := "Dimensity 7300 Pro" (Default: board platform)

# Whether Including GMS Prebuilts
WITH_GMS := true/false (Default: false)

# GMS Flavor
GMS_MAKEFILE := gms_mini.mk/gms_full/gms_pico (Default: gms_mini.mk)

# Official Build
CARPEDIEM_OFFICIAL := true/false (Default: false)

# Pixel Launcher As Default (GMS builds only)
TARGET_DEFAULT_PIXEL_LAUNCHER := true/false (Default: true)

# Background Blur Capability
TARGET_ENABLE_BLUR := true/false (Default: true)

# AOSP SetupWizard On GMS Builds (default: generic Google wizard)
TARGET_USES_AOSP_SETUPWIZARD := true/false (Default: false)

# Google PartnerSetup On GMS Builds (carrier provisioning)
TARGET_INCLUDES_PARTNERSETUP := true/false (Default: false)

# Skip Camera Apps
PRODUCT_NO_CAMERA := true/false (Default: false)
```

Custom Commands
---------------
Source the tree first (`. build/envsetup.sh`), then:
```
# Configure: carpe <device> [user|userdebug|eng] [gms|mini|full|pico|va]
# Default package is vanilla. GMS variants: gms/mini, full, pico.
carpe Galaxian userdebug gms

# Build: cb [-b|-fb|-br] [-j<num>] [user|eng|userdebug] [device]
# -b: bacon, -fb: fastboot package, -br: brunch. Plain `cb` runs `m`.
cb -b -j$(nproc --all)
```

Setup Environment:
------------------
Navigate to the root directory of Project-CarpeDiem:
```
cd path/to/source
```
Run the environment setup script:
```
. build/envsetup.sh
```
Build Configuration:
--------------------
Choose your device configuration:
```
lunch lineage_$device-$release-$buildtype
```
Replace $device with your device codename, $release with the target release
(cp2a, see `vendor/lineage/vars/aosp_target_release`) and $buildtype with your
prefered build type (user, userdebug or eng). Prefer `carpe` above, it handles
this for you.
Compilation:
------------
Start the compilation process:
```
m bacon -j$(nproc --all)
```

Submitting patches
------------------
Patches are always welcome! Please submit them via GitHub pull requests
against the `seventeen` branch of the relevant `Project-CarpeDiem` repository.

Credits
-------
CarpeDiem stands on the work of many. Base and platform: LineageOS, AOSP/Google.
Direct contributions worked in from: RisingOS-Revived (GMS tree, Personalizations
base for Ornatus, QuickSwitch core, recovery base, Lawnchair prebuilts, search
and About inspirations), Evolution-X (pixel-style resources), Pixelify-AOSP
(Launcher3 base), Project Infinity X (build command format, greetings and
device-card implementation), MaxxOS-AOSP (About port, search bar patch, shade
and blur flags). Evaluated along the way: Lunaris-AOSP, VoltageOS,
The-Clover-Project. Device maintainers and testers make releases possible.
